ky/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fzdarsky","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-et/physical-ai-platform-demo/commits/7bb54750b41c5819f7d8e9a322265c2a59b55388/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-20T15:24:20Z","email":"fzdarsky@redhat.com","name":"Frank A. Zdarsky"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-20T16:26:21Z","email":"13062727+fzdarsky@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Frank Zdarsky"},"message":"feat(pi05): add warmup inference and Triton kernel cache persistence\n\nRun a dummy inference before the WebSocket server accepts connections,\npreventing Triton max-autotune compilation from happening on the first\nreal client request (~6 min delay). Persist compiled kernels to a PVC\nso subsequent pod startups skip autotuning entirely (165s vs 341s).\n\n- Add serve_with_warmup.py wrapper with config-family registry\n  (droid/aloha/libero observation schemas)\n- Add 1Gi PVC for Triton/torch inductor cache at /cache\n- Update ServingRuntime to use warmup wrapper and cache env vars\n\nAssisted-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ba6435b2afaaa77bd8f5b5133fb0b0b94e51d31c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-et/physical-ai-platform-demo/git/trees/ba6435b2afaaa77bd8f5b5133fb0b0b94e51d31c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/redhat-et/physical-ai-platform-demo/git/commits/7bb54750b41c5819f7d8e9a322265c2a59b55388","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13062727?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fzdarsky/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fzdarsky/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fzdarsky/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fzdarsky/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fzdarsky","id":13062727,"login":"fzda