nt":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T17:11:41Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"message":" bugs","tree":{"sha":"acc36407e35ca2dbaff2f5df234b56239613b0c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/trees/acc36407e35ca2dbaff2f5df234b56239613b0c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/commits/bfbe6ff3a186f62b7a1aea3e1e981b89753962d8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/bfbe6ff3a186f62b7a1aea3e1e981b89753962d8","node_id":"C_kwDOTDGIntoAKGJmYmU2ZmYzYTE4NmY2MmI3YTFhZWEzZTFlOTgxYjg5NzUzOTYyZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/978bb1d44b9fec00e344c0759c9384bbd8e759b6","sha":"978bb1d44b9fec00e344c0759c9384bbd8e759b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/978bb1d44b9fec00e344c0759c9384bbd8e759b6"}],"sha":"bfbe6ff3a186f62b7a1aea3e1e981b89753962d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/bfbe6ff3a186f62b7a1aea3e1e981b89753962d8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/978bb1d44b9fec00e344c0759c9384bbd8e759b6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T06:12:21Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T06:12:21Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"message":"feat(pdf-tools): page transforms + document utilities, Sejda parity round 2\n\nAdds 7 new tools, completing Sejda-parity batch 2/2 (page stamping shipped\nin 9d3c82b was batch 1):\n\nPage transforms (lossless, embedPage+drawPage — text/vectors preserved):\n- Crop PDF: per-side margins via setCropBox, live preview overlay\n- Resize PDF: A4/Letter/Legal/custom target, fit-or-stretch scaling\n- Flip PDF: horizontal/vertical mirror via negative-scale affine transform\n\nRasterized (necessarily lossy, same honest caveat pattern as compress):\n- Grayscale PDF: BT.601 luminance desaturation, reuses renderPageToCanvas\n\nDocument utilities:\n- Extract Images: pulls DCTDecode (JPEG) streams via low-level pdf-lib API,\n  byte-for-byte lossless\n- Edit Metadata: title/author/subject/keywords/creator/producer, read+write\n- Remove Annotations: strips comments/markup, preserves Widget (form\n  fields) and Link annotations by design\n\nBug fixes found during verification, not requested but shipped because the\nbrief was \"without any bug\":\n\n- Edit Metadata silently corrupted Producer on save. pdf-lib''s\n  PDFDocument.load() defaults to updateMetadata: true, which stamps its own\n  Producer signature as a side effect of merely loading — before the tool\n  ever reads or writes anything. That made readPdfMetadata() report a lie\n  (pdf-lib''s stamp instead of the file''s real Producer) and made\n  setPdfMetadata() silently overwrite the true value for anyone who saved\n  without touching that field. Fixed with a metadata-preserving loader\n  (updateMetadata: false) used by both functions.\n\n- 11 single-file tools (5 pre-existing/round-1 + 6 new) used useFileList''s\n  `add` (append) instead of `replace` with multiple={false} FileDrop, so\n  dropping a second file didn''t actually replace the first — silently kept\n  operating on stale data. Verified by reproducing in-browser, then fixed\n  across the board: UnlockPdf, WatermarkPdf, PageNumbersPdf,\n  HeaderFooterPdf, BatesNumberingPdf, plus the 6 tools this commit adds.\n\nVerification (all via real content/structure inspection, not just UI):\n- Crop: page.getCropBox() matched hand-computed margins exactly\n- Resize: output page size == exact A4 points (595.28×841.89)\n- Flip: decoded content-stream transform matrix, confirmed net affine\n  equals x''=W-x (horizontal) / y''=H-y (vertical)\n- Grayscale: sampled a rendered red pixel, got RGB(76,76,76) == 0.299×255\n- Extract Images: byte-perfect JPEG round-trip (SOI/EOI markers, size)\n- Edit Metadata: full round-trip incl. regression test for the Producer bug\n- Remove Annotations: confirmed via pdfjs — Text comment removed, Link kept\n\n51 prerendered tool pages now (up from 44). typecheck/test/build all clean.","tree":{"sha":"c2ffdf228d21cc8c987f559f39c33f926322ee0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/trees/c2ffdf228d21cc8c987f559f39c33f926322ee0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/commits/978bb1d44b9fec00e344c0759c9384bbd8e759b6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/978bb1d44b9fec00e344c0759c9384bbd8e759b6","node_id":"C_kwDOTDGIntoAKDk3OGJiMWQ0NGI5ZmVjMDBlMzQ0YzA3NTljOTM4NGJiZDhlNzU5YjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/9d3c82b37086585eccc397fc1c9085112a2f9e01","sha":"9d3c82b37086585eccc397fc1c9085112a2f9e01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/9d3c82b37086585eccc397fc1c9085112a2f9e01"}],"sha":"978bb1d44b9fec00e344c0759c9384bbd8e759b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/978bb1d44b9fec00e344c0759c9384bbd8e759b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/9d3c82b37086585eccc397fc1c9085112a2f9e01/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:31:19Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T16:31:19Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"message":"feat(pdf-toolkit): add Watermark, Page Numbers, Header & Footer, Bates Numbering\n\nAdds four page-stamping tools to the PDF toolkit, matching Sejda''s own\nmenu (user shared a screenshot of Sejda''s full tool list and asked for\nfeature parity, starting with this batch by explicit priority choice).\n\nChecked each tool live on Sejda before building, not guessing at scope:\n- Watermark: text/image modes, centered/custom position, opacity,\n  rotation, font/color, page range. Built the text-watermark path (image\n  watermark and the batch/template features are out of scope for this\n  pass).\n- Page Numbers: confirmed by testing Sejda''s own editor that \"PDF Page\n  Numbers\" and \"Header & Footer\" are literally the same underlying tool\n  under two landing pages -- own numbering-format picker (1,2,3 / roman\n  / \"N of total\"), 6-position dropdown, start-from, matches its UI.\n  Header & Footer instead ships as a genuinely separate tool here since\n  Sejda''s own menu (the screenshot) lists them separately, but shares\n  the same engine.\n- Header & Footer: six independent zones (header/footer x left/center/\n  right) with {page}/{pages} tokens.\n- Bates Numbering: prefix + zero-padded sequence + suffix, matching\n  Sejda''s own \"Exhibit 1 Case XYZ 000001\" style customize-style UI.\n\nAll four share one new engine, libs/tools-core/src/pdf-stamp.ts:\nstampPages() draws formatted text at a named position (6 header/footer\nzones + center) on selected pages, reusing the existing\nparsePageRanges() rather than duplicating range-parsing logic. Each\ntool supplies its own text-formatting closure (a fixed string for\nWatermark, a per-page sequence for the numbering tools) -- the position\nmath, font embedding and opacity/rotation handling live in exactly one\nplace. Small helpers (toRomanNumeral, zeroPad, formatPageNumberText)\nare also exported for reuse/testing.\n\nShared UI fields (position/font-family/font-size/color/page-range\npickers) live in apps/pdf-tools/src/tools/stamp-controls.tsx so the\nfour tool components stay focused on their own specific fields.\n\nVerified end-to-end for all four -- not just that the UI renders, but\nthat the actual exported PDF''s content stream is correct -- by\ndecoding each result''s real PDF operators after running it through the\nbrowser:\n- Watermark: \"CONFIDENTIAL\" in red (1 0 0 rg), a cos45/sin45 rotation\n  matrix, and an ExtGState reference for the 35% opacity, on every page\n  of a 2-page test file.\n- Page Numbers: \"Page 1\" / \"Page 2\" at the correct bottom-center\n  position and black color on their respective pages.\n- Bates Numbering: \"ABC000001\" / \"ABC000002\", zero-padded to 6 digits,\n  at bottom-right.\n- Header & Footer: \"My Document\" in the header-left zone on both pages,\n  and \"Page 1 of 2\" / \"Page 2 of 2\" in footer-center with {page}/\n  {pages} tokens correctly resolved against the real page count.\n\nAlso confirmed via the shell''s own dev server that all four appear\ncorrectly in the PDF Toolkit sidebar under a new \"Transform\" category,\nand that postbuild''s prerender count moved from 40 to 44 pages.\nnpm run typecheck/test/build all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b79517ee404f2d4da19f4e599c2767d9e3dc5fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/trees/7b79517ee404f2d4da19f4e599c2767d9e3dc5fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/commits/9d3c82b37086585eccc397fc1c9085112a2f9e01","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/9d3c82b37086585eccc397fc1c9085112a2f9e01","node_id":"C_kwDOTDGIntoAKDlkM2M4MmIzNzA4NjU4NWVjY2MzOTdmYzFjOTA4NTExMmEyZjllMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/b735602a9290d90b31678dc8be4410c045180bb9","sha":"b735602a9290d90b31678dc8be4410c045180bb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/b735602a9290d90b31678dc8be4410c045180bb9"}],"sha":"9d3c82b37086585eccc397fc1c9085112a2f9e01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/9d3c82b37086585eccc397fc1c9085112a2f9e01"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/b735602a9290d90b31678dc8be4410c045180bb9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T10:33:24Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-09T10:33:24Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"message":"fix(edit-pdf): colored background vanishing to white on existing-text edit, plus stray blank-text clicks\n\nReported: \"when we edit colorful pdf original color is vanishing\" (with\na screenshot of a pink-background section whose whiteout patch rendered\nplain white), and repeated stray \"(empty)\" text boxes littering the page\nfrom misses on click-to-edit.\n\nTwo bugs behind the color report, found by instrumenting the actual\nrunning code rather than guessing:\n\n1. sampleRunColors() sampled the background from a single fixed pixel\n   3px diagonally outside the text run''s box. That''s fragile by\n   construction -- easy to overshoot past a colored section''s own edge\n   into the plain page background, or land on adjacent text. Replaced\n   with a majority-color vote across the run''s own bounding box (plus a\n   small margin): normal text has far more inter-glyph/inter-line\n   background than ink, so the largest color bucket reliably is the\n   background, sampled from the exact same colored region the text\n   lives in -- can''t overshoot into a neighboring section anymore.\n\n2. The real reason the screenshot still showed white even where sampling\n   was already correct: WhiteoutAnnotationView''s <rect> had\n   fill=\"#FFFFFF\" hardcoded, ignoring annotation.color entirely. The\n   *exported* PDF was already right -- drawWhiteout() in pdf-edit.ts\n   correctly used ann.color -- this was purely a live-preview bug, but\n   an important one: what you see while editing didn''t match either the\n   original page or the eventual download.\n\nAlso hardened findRunAt() (textSearch.ts) with a small tolerance around\neach run''s tight glyph box instead of an exact match: pdf.js splits text\ninto a separate run per style change, so there are often small real gaps\nbetween runs on the same line, and a run''s vertical box is tighter than\nthe visually \"clickable\" line. An ordinary click landing in one of those\ngaps missed every run and fell through to \"place new blank text\" --\nexactly the stray \"(empty)\" boxes reported. Ties among overlapping\npadded regions are broken by proximity to each run''s own unpadded box,\nso an exact hit always wins over a near-miss on some other run''s\npadding. This only ever *expands* what a click can hit, so it can''t\nregress any click that was already landing correctly.\n\nVerified end-to-end: instrumented getImageData calls to confirm the\nsampled region and majority-bucket color exactly matched a hand-built\nPDF with a pink section (#f2cfd3, matching the section''s actual fill),\nconfirmed the previous code''s single-pixel sample landed on the right\nspot too (so the *sampling* was already fine) while the rendered rect\nstill showed white -- isolating the bug to the hardcoded fill -- then\nconfirmed the fix: the same click now renders the correct pink,\nmatching the section around it. npm run typecheck/test/build all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d6a5d18aef30c49ea73d7809662016d211d1cbcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/trees/d6a5d18aef30c49ea73d7809662016d211d1cbcd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/commits/b735602a9290d90b31678dc8be4410c045180bb9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/b735602a9290d90b31678dc8be4410c045180bb9","node_id":"C_kwDOTDGIntoAKGI3MzU2MDJhOTI5MGQ5MGIzMTY3OGRjOGJlNDQxMGMwNDUxODBiYjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/00c8ffdc3c0e7a53738e36a8bac7cc2343939ed7","sha":"00c8ffdc3c0e7a53738e36a8bac7cc2343939ed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/00c8ffdc3c0e7a53738e36a8bac7cc2343939ed7"}],"sha":"b735602a9290d90b31678dc8be4410c045180bb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/b735602a9290d90b31678dc8be4410c045180bb9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/00c8ffdc3c0e7a53738e36a8bac7cc2343939ed7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:13:32Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:13:32Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"message":"fix(edit-pdf): existing-text font matching wrongly picked Times for sans-serif documents\n\nReported (with a screenshot of a resume, clearly sans-serif throughout):\n\"font when we edit it has to adjust with existing original color not\nother color or font style font-variation should not other, it has to\nalign with original font.\"\n\nRoot cause: matchStandardFont()''s serif-detection regex tested for the\nliteral substring \"serif\" -- which is also the tail end of \"sans-serif\",\npdf.js''s own generic CSS fallback for any embedded font it can''t\nidentify more specifically. That''s not a rare edge case; it''s the\ncommon case for anything exported from a resume builder, Google Docs,\nWord, etc. -- exactly the kind of document in the report''s screenshot.\nEvery plain sans-serif document with an unidentified font was getting\nits replacement text matched to Times, backwards from \"best-effort\nmatch the original font\" (design doc S3).\n\nFixed by checking for \"sans\" (and common sans typeface names -- Arial,\nHelvetica, Calibri, Verdana, Segoe, Roboto, etc.) before the serif\ncheck, so \"sans-serif\" and font-stack strings like\n\"ABCDEF+Calibri-Bold, sans-serif\" resolve to Helvetica the way they\nshould; genuine serif hints (\"Georgia, serif\", \"Times New Roman\") are\nunaffected. This is the one field that actually drives the exported\nPDF''s font (flattenAnnotations'' getFont() reads fontFamily, not any\nother signal), so this fixes both the on-screen preview and the final\ndownloaded file, not just the toolbar''s dropdown.\n\nVerified: a battery of realistic pdf.js-style hints (bare \"sans-serif\",\n\"Arial, sans-serif\", \"Calibri\", embedded-subset patterns like\n\"ABCDEF+Calibri-Bold, sans-serif\") all now resolve to Helvetica (with\nBold/Italic still correctly detected), while true serif hints still\nresolve to Times. Re-tested the same Helvetica-drawn test PDF used\nthroughout this session''s QA -- previously mismatched to \"Times\n(serif)\" in the toolbar, now correctly shows \"Helvetica\". npm run\ntypecheck/test/build all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e2b35813876e912017d3c966cacb5d573047cbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/trees/0e2b35813876e912017d3c966cacb5d573047cbf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/commits/00c8ffdc3c0e7a53738e36a8bac7cc2343939ed7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/00c8ffdc3c0e7a53738e36a8bac7cc2343939ed7","node_id":"C_kwDOTDGIntoAKDAwYzhmZmRjM2MwZTdhNTM3MzhlMzZhOGJhYzdjYzIzNDM5MzllZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/1a1a54e7c4dcb3ef213b2d3cf687f4d8c18a762b","sha":"1a1a54e7c4dcb3ef213b2d3cf687f4d8c18a762b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/1a1a54e7c4dcb3ef213b2d3cf687f4d8c18a762b"}],"sha":"00c8ffdc3c0e7a53738e36a8bac7cc2343939ed7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/00c8ffdc3c0e7a53738e36a8bac7cc2343939ed7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/1a1a54e7c4dcb3ef213b2d3cf687f4d8c18a762b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T07:54:59Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T07:55:20Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"message":"fix(edit-pdf): floating toolbar overlapping the selected text\n\nReported: \"edit text on hover coming border properly but when i click\ntoolbar is overlaying on that text.\"\n\nTwo compounding bugs, found by testing at viewport widths where the page\nframe actually renders smaller than its nominal pixel size (the\nresponsive max-width:100% shrinking from an earlier fix):\n\n1. ElementToolbar positioned itself using a hardcoded single-row height\n   estimate (34px). Text''s floating toolbar (family/size/Bold/Italic/\n   color/background, from the last round of fixes) is often wide enough\n   to wrap onto 2-3 rows, so placing it \"above\" the text using the wrong\n   (too small) height put its lower rows right on top of the text.\n   Fixed by measuring the toolbar''s own real rendered height after each\n   render (useLayoutEffect, settling in one corrective render, matching\n   the same pattern already used for the auto-growing text input) and\n   positioning from that instead of a constant.\n\n2. The deeper bug: ElementToolbar''s box.sx/sy (from getAnnotationScreenBox)\n   are in the SVG''s nominal viewBox coordinate space, correct for anything\n   drawn inside the SVG (the browser''s own viewBox transform scales those\n   to real pixels for free) but wrong when used as raw left/top CSS pixels\n   for a plain HTML div outside the SVG, which is exactly what\n   ElementToolbar is. This was silently correct only when the page frame\n   happened to render at exactly its nominal pixel size -- at any width\n   where CSS legitimately shrinks the frame (confirmed: 918px nominal ->\n   620px actual at a 700px viewport), both the horizontal and vertical\n   position were off by the frame''s scale factor, on top of bug #1.\n   Added scaleScreenBox() in geometry.ts and a frameScale state tracked\n   via ResizeObserver on the page''s own <svg> element (EditPdf.tsx) -- the\n   same nominal-to-real conversion getPointerPos already does per-event,\n   now available during render and kept correct across window resizes and\n   zoom changes. Also widened the toolbar''s own max-width (28rem -> 40rem)\n   so it wraps less often on typical desktop widths, closer to how\n   Sejda''s own toolbar stays a single row.\n\nVerified with real clicks at multiple viewport widths (700px and 1280px,\nplus resizing 700->1280 while a text stays selected, which exercises the\nResizeObserver path): toolbar-to-text gap measured exactly 6px (the\nintended GAP) with zero overlap in every case, both when the toolbar\nrenders above and when it falls back to below (no room above).\nnpm run typecheck/test/build all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e51788ea5ea451b8c89efe5a48363460e552d5fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/trees/e51788ea5ea451b8c89efe5a48363460e552d5fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/commits/1a1a54e7c4dcb3ef213b2d3cf687f4d8c18a762b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/1a1a54e7c4dcb3ef213b2d3cf687f4d8c18a762b","node_id":"C_kwDOTDGIntoAKDFhMWE1NGU3YzRkY2IzZWYyMTNiMmQzY2Y2ODdmNGQ4YzE4YTc2MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/9f45f37196dfe94de6a819baee39e8611a8e2b2a","sha":"9f45f37196dfe94de6a819baee39e8611a8e2b2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/9f45f37196dfe94de6a819baee39e8611a8e2b2a"}],"sha":"1a1a54e7c4dcb3ef213b2d3cf687f4d8c18a762b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/1a1a54e7c4dcb3ef213b2d3cf687f4d8c18a762b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/9f45f37196dfe94de6a819baee39e8611a8e2b2a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T07:27:26Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T07:27:26Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"message":"fix(edit-pdf): single-line auto-growing text box, matching Sejda exactly\n\nRe-checked Sejda''s live editor more carefully after the last round of\nfixes and found the biggest remaining gap: its text box is a single-line\nfield that only grows in width as you type — confirmed directly against\nsejda.com by typing a long sentence into its own text-editable div\n(width grew 124px -> 717px, height never changed) and pressing Enter\nmid-sentence (no new line — the next characters just kept appending to\nthe same line).\n\nOurs was a large fixed-size multi-line <textarea> inside a foreignObject\nsized Math.max(measuredWidth+40,220) x Math.max(measuredHeight*4,90) —\nwrapping text and offering room for several lines regardless of content,\nwhich looks and behaves nothing like Sejda''s tight single-line field.\n\nReplaced the <textarea> with a plain <input type=\"text\">, sized every\nrender from the same textAnnotationScreenBox()/measureText() the\nselection outline already uses (see the previous commit), so the\nforeignObject naturally grows in width with each keystroke and never\ngrows taller. Enter now commits (blurs) the field instead of doing\nnothing, matching every other single-line input in this editor (the\nlink/field-name inputs already commit on Enter) — a deliberate small\nimprovement over Sejda''s own inert Enter, not a regression from it.\n\nVerified end-to-end with fully genuine (non-synthetic) clicks in the\nstandalone dev harness: typed a 55-character sentence via real key\nevents and watched the foreignObject width grow 89.77px -> 522.89px\nwhile height stayed fixed at 31.2px (one line), then committed via a\nreal click elsewhere and confirmed both test annotations rendered at\ntheir full, unclipped width (625px and 504px measured via\ngetBoundingClientRect). npm run typecheck/test/build all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4933691a671ecf5b6c5efb40916198ff4d3da1f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/trees/4933691a671ecf5b6c5efb40916198ff4d3da1f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/commits/9f45f37196dfe94de6a819baee39e8611a8e2b2a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/9f45f37196dfe94de6a819baee39e8611a8e2b2a","node_id":"C_kwDOTDGIntoAKDlmNDVmMzcxOTZkZmU5NGRlNmE4MTliYWVlMzllODYxMWE4ZTJiMmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/2fc7df5df379e7910242fc20ba0573f40a82a505","sha":"2fc7df5df379e7910242fc20ba0573f40a82a505","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/2fc7df5df379e7910242fc20ba0573f40a82a505"}],"sha":"9f45f37196dfe94de6a819baee39e8611a8e2b2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/9f45f37196dfe94de6a819baee39e8611a8e2b2a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/2fc7df5df379e7910242fc20ba0573f40a82a505/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T05:37:47Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T05:37:47Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"message":"fix(edit-pdf): default to Text tool, tight text outline, rich text toolbar, auto-download\n\nRe-checked the live Sejda editor (sejda.com/pdf-editor) against ours and\nclosed four concrete gaps:\n\n1. Default tool was \"select\"; Sejda opens with \"Text\" active by default\n   (click any existing text to edit it, click blank space to place new\n   text) — confirmed via Sejda''s own DOM (Text button carries\n   active/active-sticky on load).\n\n2. The text annotation''s selection/hover outline used a fixed per-character\n   heuristic (length * fontSize * 0.55 + padding) that always drew looser\n   than the actual glyphs. Replaced with real canvas text measurement\n   (measureText.ts) shared between the outline and the floating toolbar''s\n   position (textAnnotationScreenBox in elements.tsx), plus a genuine hover\n   affordance (not just selected) matching Sejda''s contenteditable-div\n   outline, which is exactly its rendered content with near-zero padding.\n\n3. Selecting a text annotation only offered Duplicate/Delete. Sejda''s own\n   floating toolbar has font family, size, Bold, Italic, and color controls\n   (confirmed via its CSS classes: font-bold-opts, font-italic-opts,\n   several dropdown-toggles). Added TextToolbarControls.tsx with all of\n   that, plus a background-color control for the existing-text patch\n   pipeline''s paired whiteout (new optional TextAnnotation.coverId links\n   the two). Bold/Italic/family write through fontFamily (composed via new\n   fontMatch.ts helpers) rather than the annotation''s separate bold/italic\n   booleans, which flattenAnnotations already ignored entirely at export\n   time — those fields were dead until now.\n\n4. \"Apply changes\" left a \"PDF saved\" note requiring a second manual\n   Download click. Sejda''s own flow downloads as soon as the result is\n   ready. Added an effect that auto-triggers the download the moment a new\n   result lands, keeping the manual Download button as a re-save option.\n\nVerified end-to-end against a real PDF in the standalone dev harness:\ndefault tool confirmed Text, existing-text click produces a tight\nmeasured outline (numerically ~22% narrower than the old formula) with\nfamily/size/Bold/Italic/text-color/background-color all present and\nfunctional, and Apply changes auto-downloads a valid PDF (verified via\ncaptured Blob: %PDF-1.7 header, correct size/mime) without a second click.\nnpm run typecheck/test/build all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a702dd596b3eebdea33e8e572d08dce46f971e5e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/trees/a702dd596b3eebdea33e8e572d08dce46f971e5e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/commits/2fc7df5df379e7910242fc20ba0573f40a82a505","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/2fc7df5df379e7910242fc20ba0573f40a82a505","node_id":"C_kwDOTDGIntoAKDJmYzdkZjVkZjM3OWU3OTEwMjQyZmMyMGJhMDU3M2Y0MGE4MmE1MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/9329786fbaed4655e4434852d61932c2430a6fa4","sha":"9329786fbaed4655e4434852d61932c2430a6fa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/9329786fbaed4655e4434852d61932c2430a6fa4"}],"sha":"2fc7df5df379e7910242fc20ba0573f40a82a505","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/2fc7df5df379e7910242fc20ba0573f40a82a505"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/9329786fbaed4655e4434852d61932c2430a6fa4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T15:07:01Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T15:07:01Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"message":"fix(edit-pdf): resolve horizontal overflow on mobile/narrow viewports\n\nThe editor''s page canvas overflowed the viewport on narrow screens.\nRoot cause was two-fold:\n\n1. .pdfed__page and .pdfed__pageframe used a JS-computed inline pixel\n   width (zoomed page size) with only max-width:100% to clamp it, but\n   percentage max-width can''t constrain a shrink-to-fit flex item''s\n   intrinsic width (viewport''s align-items:center). Gave .pdfed__page\n   a definite width:100% so descendants'' max-width:100% has something\n   to resolve against.\n\n2. The real culprit: on mobile, .pdfed__body switches to\n   flex-direction:column so the thumbnail rail stacks above the page\n   viewport, but its unconditional align-items:flex-start (meant for\n   the desktop row layout''s vertical alignment) became a width\n   shrink-to-fit rule once the axis flipped, so .pdfed__viewport never\n   filled the container and let the 918px page leak through. Added\n   align-items:stretch to the mobile .pdfed__body override.\n\nVerified via browser: no horizontal overflow at 375px (mobile),\n768px (tablet, at the breakpoint), or 1280px (desktop); desktop page\ncentering and full-width PageChrome unchanged; page-thumbnails panel\nopen on mobile also clean. npm run typecheck/test/build all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3898e12061b379137cad708e3e539ccd5b727f57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/trees/3898e12061b379137cad708e3e539ccd5b727f57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/commits/9329786fbaed4655e4434852d61932c2430a6fa4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/9329786fbaed4655e4434852d61932c2430a6fa4","node_id":"C_kwDOTDGIntoAKDkzMjk3ODZmYmFlZDQ2NTVlNDQzNDg1MmQ2MTkzMmMyNDMwYTZmYTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/95ac3ef8ef47a0aa588082b39faffafb7dfa62ae","sha":"95ac3ef8ef47a0aa588082b39faffafb7dfa62ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/95ac3ef8ef47a0aa588082b39faffafb7dfa62ae"}],"sha":"9329786fbaed4655e4434852d61932c2430a6fa4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/9329786fbaed4655e4434852d61932c2430a6fa4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/95ac3ef8ef47a0aa588082b39faffafb7dfa62ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-07T14:19:04Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-07T14:19:04Z","email":"shashikanth033@gmail.com","name":"shashikanth077"},"message":"feat(edit-pdf): best-effort existing-text edit (Phase 4)\n\nClicking with the Text tool now hit-tests the current page''s extracted\ntext runs before falling back to placing a blank text box (findRunAt in\ntextSearch.ts). A hit commits the same whiteout-cover + text-overlay pair\nFind & Replace already uses (one undo step via the new addTextPatch),\npre-filled with the run''s own text and opened for editing immediately —\nstill strictly additive to the content stream, same safety story as\nevery other tool here (design doc §3).\n\nTwo additions make the patch look closer to the original than a plain\nwhite box + black Helvetica:\n- colorSample.ts: reads ink and background color straight off the\n  already-rendered page <img> via an offscreen canvas — synchronous, no\n  extra image load, since the img is already decoded and on screen by\n  the time a click can happen.\n- fontMatch.ts: maps pdf.js''s own font-family guess for the run onto the\n  closest of pdf-lib''s 14 standard fonts by serif/sans/mono + bold/italic\n  keyword matching. Threaded through to both the live editor''s on-screen\n  preview (matching web-safe CSS stack) and the real embedded font at\n  export (pdf-edit.ts now embeds fonts lazily per distinct name instead\n  of a single fixed Helvetica).\n\nRotated/vertical text runs are excluded from hit-testing rather than\npatched — clicking one just places new text on top like any blank spot,\nwhich is the disclosure: nothing claims to have edited what it didn''t.\n\nVerified end to end: clicking real body text opens it pre-filled with a\ncorrectly matched font; after editing and exporting, PDFDocument.load()\nround-trips cleanly and page.getTextContent() on the saved file shows\nboth the original run (still present underneath, as documented) and the\nnew text.\n\nnpm run typecheck, npm test, and npm run build all pass. This completes\nall four phases scoped in the design doc.","tree":{"sha":"c7cad800b1a406242d63228412f7c49a7467e848","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/trees/c7cad800b1a406242d63228412f7c49a7467e848"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/git/commits/95ac3ef8ef47a0aa588082b39faffafb7dfa62ae","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3NzQ0NzA5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/95ac3ef8ef47a0aa588082b39faffafb7dfa62ae","node_id":"C_kwDOTDGIntoAKDk1YWMzZWY4ZWY0N2EwYWE1ODgwODJiMzlmYWZmYWZiN2RmYTYyYWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commit/991b0db563bff81e527d27bfdc82982a9d2f82a1","sha":"991b0db563bff81e527d27bfdc82982a9d2f82a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/991b0db563bff81e527d27bfdc82982a9d2f82a1"}],"sha":"95ac3ef8ef47a0aa588082b39faffafb7dfa62ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/shashikanth077/shashikanth077.github.io/commits/95ac3ef8ef47a0aa588082b39faffafb7dfa62ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/57744709?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/shashikanth077/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/shashikanth077","id":57744709,"login":"shashikanth077","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlc