ithub.com/users/juicycleff/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juicycleff/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juicycleff/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/juicycleff/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juicycleff","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xraph/fabriq-admin/commits/83382a952ef56444e215612e2c78d9682ba8ba26/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T16:42:02Z","email":"rex.raphael@outlook.com","name":"Rex Raphael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T16:42:02Z","email":"rex.raphael@outlook.com","name":"Rex Raphael"},"message":"fix(plugin-analytics): guard followJob fallback poll, add stream/concurrency test coverage\n\n- followJob''s fallback poll (from both the confirm-read path and the SSE\n  catch) now wraps pollJob in its own try/catch and surfaces a transient\n  error once via setRunErr instead of silently re-entering pollJob with a\n  fresh budget, matching the tenants JobFollower shape.\n- Test harness makeClient gains an optional streamEvents opt so stream()\n  can yield real events; default (no-events) behavior is unchanged. Adds\n  a test exercising the primary stream-consumption branch directly, plus\n  a test locking in that an empty/absent concurrency never lands in the\n  fleet-op request body.\n- Reworded the analyticsJobStream doc comment to make clear it supersedes\n  analyticsJobStreamUrl rather than the other way around.","tree":{"sha":"d08c89d0b3c66b7e0774b53f0d057df68c8dd2b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xraph/fabriq-admin/git/trees/d08c89d0b3c66b7e0774b53f0d057df68c8dd2b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/xraph/fabriq-admin/git/commits/83382a952ef56444e215612e2c78d9682ba8ba26","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u