hub.com/users/sdkwork-ai","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-iam/commits/615de7226e7cc4286bd555ec5584974c60279659/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:37:27Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T18:37:27Z","email":"sdkwork@zowalk.com","name":"sdkwork-ai"},"message":"feat(iam-commerce): register fine-grained payment permission codes\n\nThe payment backend OpenAPI declares per-family\nx-sdkwork-permission codes (refunds.create, provider_accounts.credentials.rotate,\nwebhook_events.replay, ...) and the payment route manifest now enforces\nthem via ManifestAuthorizationPolicy. The commerce module catalog only\ncarried the coarse commerce.payments.manage/read pair, so no principal\ncould hold the fine codes except wildcard holders. Register all 40 codes\n(resource family + action) so roles can grant per-family access, and\nbump catalogVersion to 1.1.0. Standard roles keep working: they grant\nthe commerce.payments.* prefix, which permission_matches expands over\nthe new codes.","tree":{"sha":"a6c857e9ce20ffd6aa5e7838dc3a8033bc0665b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-iam/git/trees/a6c857e9ce20ffd6aa5e7838dc3a8033bc0665b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sdkwork-ai/sdkwork-iam/git/commits/615de7226e7cc4286bd555ec5584974c60279659","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/218460407?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sdkwork-ai/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sdkwork-ai","id":218460407,"login":"sdkwork-ai","node_id":"U_kgDODQV