/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EijiYoshimura/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EijiYoshimura","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EijiYoshimura/jogo-memoria/commits/b7e856f455f35a768a04686ac83c5018e75cc744/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-08T00:49:06Z","email":"eiji@eijiyoshimura.com.br","name":"Eiji Yoshimura"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-08T00:49:06Z","email":"eiji@eijiyoshimura.com.br","name":"Eiji Yoshimura"},"message":"docs(HUB-149/HUB-150): corrige premissas — CPF só formatado (não oculto) e ADR-015 com duas chamadas sequenciais\n\nDuas correções do stakeholder sobre a entrega anterior:\n1. \"Mascarar o CPF\" significa apenas formatação com pontuação (123.456.789-00),\n   não redação parcial. ADR-014 deixa de reverter a ADR-013 e passa a complementá-la\n   — o CPF continua 100% completo em todo CSV. Resolve por completo o risco de\n   perda de trilha auditável após a Limpeza de Leads e a lacuna do Table Editor.\n2. ADR-015: o stakeholder rejeitou a RPC atômica recomendada pelo Tech Lead e optou\n   por manter duas chamadas sequenciais (export, depois delete), ciente e aceitando\n   conscientemente o risco residual de janela de corrida entre as duas chamadas.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"542a9c8bc0f9857827a2a726bcea9a36a75758be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EijiYoshimura/jogo-memoria/git/trees/542a9c8bc0f9857827a2a726bcea9a36a75758be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EijiYoshimura/jogo-memoria/git/commits/b7e856f455f35a768a04686ac83c5018e75cc744","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/55535598?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EijiYoshimura/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/EijiYoshimura/followers","followi